================================================================================
Search programs built into the koda binary (koda-search)
================================================================================

The koda binary contains ugrep and bfs, compiled from their sources, as
Claude Code's executable contains them. The sources are vendored unchanged
under koda-search/vendor/, each folder with its upstream license file and a
.commit file naming the release:

  ugrep 7.8.5 (with RE/flex and 7-Zip's decoder)
      koda-search/vendor/ugrep, BSD 3-Clause License,
      https://github.com/Genivia/ugrep
  bfs 4.1.7
      koda-search/vendor/bfs, BSD Zero Clause License (0BSD),
      https://github.com/tavianator/bfs
  PCRE2 10.49 (with SLJIT)
      koda-search/vendor/pcre2, BSD 3-Clause License with the PCRE2
      exception, https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2
  Oniguruma 6.9.10
      koda-search/vendor/oniguruma, BSD 2-Clause License,
      https://github.com/kkos/oniguruma
  Brotli 1.2.1 (decoder)
      koda-search/vendor/brotli, MIT License,
      https://github.com/google/brotli

zlib, bzip2 and zstd are linked from the libz-sys, bzip2-sys and zstd-sys
crates, under the zlib, bzip2 and BSD 3-Clause licenses. The release archives
carry these license texts in licenses/.
